*.jsonl
debug/
cache/
telemetry/
session-env/
*.log
.DS_Store

# Scratch/working dirs — never committed. tmp/ holds god-review findings,
# pre-compact briefs, ready-plans, etc. that often contain fixture strings
# tripping the secret-scan and shouldn't be auto-pushed anyway.
tmp/

# Secrets — never commit
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
credentials.md
credentials.local.md
# R3 D5: glob covers CLAUDE.local.md (alias), CLAUDE.local.<sid8>.md (SID-tagged primary),
# CLAUDE.local.md.prev (snapshot), and future .tmp variants.
# Pattern: CLAUDE.local*.md* — wildcard after .local covers SID8 segment; trailing * covers
# .prev suffix on the alias. Matches: CLAUDE.local.md, CLAUDE.local.18d1779a.md,
# CLAUDE.local.md.prev. The original **/CLAUDE.local.md* did NOT match SID-tagged files.
**/CLAUDE.local*.md*

# Common secret-bearing files (defense in depth)
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa
id_rsa.*
id_ed25519
id_ed25519.*
id_ecdsa
id_ecdsa.*
.ssh/
# (the root-anchored `.aws/credentials` and `.aws/config` that used to sit here were REPLACED
#  by the depth-matching `**/` forms below - one rule per intent, not two)
.gcp/
*.credentials.json
credentials.json
*service-account*.json
*-key.json
.netrc
# 2026-08-03 round-2 review: these two were the SAME root-anchoring defect the note at the
# bottom of this file documents, sitting three lines above it. MEASURED before the fix:
# `sub/.aws/credentials` and `deep/x/.aws/config` were NOT ignored. `.aws/config` is the
# sharper of the two - it carries no AKIA-shaped token, so the scanner lane offered as the
# alternate cover does not fire either, making a nested checkout a path BOTH layers assume
# the other is handling.
**/.aws/credentials
**/.aws/config
# git's own credential-store writes PLAINTEXT `https://user:password@host` lines here, and
# the scanner deliberately excludes credential URLs (too many false positives on ordinary
# URLs), so before this entry neither layer covered it. Verified NOT ignored at any depth.
.git-credentials
**/git/credentials
# Added 2026-08-03 after a god-report finding verified BOTH layers missing these.
# This repo runs `git add -A` and auto-pushes to a PUBLIC remote, so an unignored
# secret-bearing file is one `direnv allow` / `npm login` / `docker login` from exposure.
# The asymmetry that makes gitignore load-bearing here: .envrc holds an arbitrary
# `export DB_PASSWORD=<opaque>`, which NO scanner can pattern-match - so for that file this
# is the only control that can work.
#
# NOT "defense in depth" for these files, and the earlier comment claiming so was wrong:
# once a path is ignored, `--working` (which enumerates via `git ls-files --others
# --exclude-standard`) never sees it and it can never be staged, so the scanner and this
# file are MUTUALLY EXCLUSIVE here, not stacked. The npm_ lane added to secret-scan.sh is
# still worth having, but for a DIFFERENT surface: a token pasted into a doc, a commit
# message, or any non-ignored file.
#
# NOTE `*.credentials.json` above does NOT cover a bare `credentials.json` - the wildcard
# reads broader than it is, which is exactly how that one slipped through; hence the
# explicit entry added above it.
#
# NOTE every pattern here is intentionally SLASH-FREE so it matches at any depth. A pattern
# containing a slash is root-anchored: `.docker/config.json` would NOT match
# `sub/.docker/config.json`. Hence the `**/` form below.
.envrc
.npmrc
.dockercfg
**/.docker/config.json
.npmrc.local
.pypirc

# Editor / OS swap files that may contain partial buffer contents
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.#*

# Mac mini CRD skill — built Go binaries (not committed)
skills/macmini/server/dist/
skills/macmini/client/dist/

# Codex bridge — generated locally from commands/ and skills/
codex/generated/
__pycache__/
